{"type":"standard","title":"Tasawaq language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Tasawaq language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q36564","titles":{"canonical":"Tasawaq_language","normalized":"Tasawaq language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Tasawaq language</span></span>"},"pageid":32560681,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Songhay_languages.svg/330px-Songhay_languages.svg.png","width":330,"height":265},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Songhay_languages.svg/1280px-Songhay_languages.svg.png","width":1200,"height":965},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1175968086","tid":"d82f3ec5-563e-11ee-b095-4908fca5939a","timestamp":"2023-09-18T16:17:21Z","description":"Songhay language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasawaq_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasawaq_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasawaq_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Tasawaq_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasawaq_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Tasawaq_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasawaq_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Tasawaq_language"}},"extract":"Tasawaq, sometimes also called Ingelshi, is a Northern Songhay language spoken by the Issawaghan or Ingalkoyyu, a community surrounding the town of In-Gall in Niger. A closely related variety called Emghedeshie was spoken in Agadez but is now extinct.","extract_html":"<p><b>Tasawaq</b>, sometimes also called <i>Ingelshi</i>, is a Northern Songhay language spoken by the <i>Issawaghan</i> or <i>Ingalkoyyu</i>, a community surrounding the town of In-Gall in Niger. A closely related variety called Emghedeshie was spoken in Agadez but is now extinct.</p>"}